A '''Revive Stone''' is a {{Legendary}} [[Dungeon Item]] that can revive dead players when in a [[Dungeon]] run. 

== Obtaining ==
=== Mob Drops ===
A '''Revive Stone''' has a {{Chance|100%|1|1}} to drop from killing a {{MobSprite|Fairy}} while all the player's teammates are alive.

There is a {{Chance|22%|1|4.5}} chance for one drop from killing a {{MobSprite|Crypt Undead}}, as well as an additional {{Chance|100%|1|1}} chance for one to drop from killing a {{MobSprite|Prince}} version of one. 

There is also a small chance{{InfoNeeded}} for one to appear when killing every starred mob in a room.

=== Shops ===
{{NPCSprite|Winona}} sells '''Revive Stones''' in the [[Catacombs]] for {{Coins|100,000}} each. 

Additionally, the [[Undead Essence Shop]] contains the {{Green|Help of the Fairies}} perk, which grants a free '''Revive Stone''' at the start of all Dungeon runs.

== Usage ==
{{ItemInfo
|type = Item
|rarity = l
|item_ability_name = Revive
|item_ability_activation = Right Click
|item_ability_description = Revive a player who has died in a dungeon. ONE TIME USE. <br> {{Yellow|This item will disappear from your inventory at the end of the Dungeon!}}
}}

'''Revive Stone'''<nowiki />'s main purpose is to revive dead players in Dungeons. If a player with a '''Revive Stone''' dies, it is consumed in order to revive them at their location.{{InfoNeeded|Which takes priority? Healer passive, Help of the Fairies or player's Revive Stone? Does the player get revived at the respective location?}}. It is also possible to revive other players using it. If only one player is dead, right-clicking a '''Revive Stone''' consumes the item to revive them. If there are multiple, it opens a menu, where the player can choose which deceased player to revive, after which the item is consumed. The reviving process itself takes {{green|5 seconds}}.
=== Abiphone Contacts ===
Players must give {{Item|Revive Stone|amount=2}}s to obtain the [[Abiphone]] contact for {{NPCSprite|Trinity}}.

